  "rationale": "The representative prefix ends in “with”, but the model assigns nearly all probability to “a”; the small weight-only update barely changes that. Across the documents, “with” introduces a person name, and the batch also repeatedly uses “One day” alongside the already-supported “One morning.” Add modest lexical-context evidence for the available person-name tokens after “with”, plus evidence for “day” after “One”. This should improve those recurring constructions without asserting that every preposition requires a name or that “One” has only one continuation. Other uses of “with” and other continuations after “One” remain possible; the replay gate must assess whether these additions preserve earlier behavior.",
